@@ -14,6 +14,57 @@
 RBAC/ABAC/PBAC) and the development backlog.
 
 ## Install
+
+### Private human-access extension
+
+This private development patch adds optional `humans[].counterpart_persona` and
+`policies.phantomview.project_grants` metadata. These fields are not available in
+the unpatched upstream release. Omit a counterpart for an unbound human; a
+counterpart must name an existing actor and cannot be assigned to two humans.
+An email-only human can have a declared counterpart without being authenticated
+for dashboard access. `reports_to_human` remains a reporting relationship.
+
+```yaml
+humans:
+  - id: alice
+    counterpart_persona: coordinator
+    telegram_user_id: 123456789
+  - id: blair
+    counterpart_persona: treasurer
+    email: blair@example.org
+policies:
+  phantomview:
+    project_grants:
+      coordinator: [example-project]
+```
+
+These snippets extend the usual complete organization document. Project grants
+are exact identifiers assigned to existing actors; no project is inferred from
+a category number, reporting line or job title. Humans inherit their explicit
+counterpart's ordinary information scope in the PhantomView policy resolver.
+The private extension also supports explicit `scope_definitions`,
+`persona_scope_grants` and `human_action_grants` under `policies.phantomview`.
+Scope kinds are organization, department and project. Project scope grants need
+matching explicit project grants. Human capabilities for resource editing,
+classification, personal-view editing and shared-view editing are independent of
+read categories and category zero. Unknown references and duplicate grants are
+rejected. These fields do not install an action executor or change live access.
+The patch also preserves the optional `organization.display_name` already used
+by the private dashboard; it is a label and never changes organization identity.
+
+When the optional `policies.phantomview` block is present, validation requires a
+declared `category-0`. Its explicit `owner` must resolve by case-insensitive human
+ID or name to exactly one registered human, who need not have a counterpart.
+Omitting the owner leaves resolution to PhantomView's verified installation
+default and its unique human counterpart. The compiler never guesses that
+default. Existing actor-category semantics remain unchanged for other consumers.
+
+This metadata does not authenticate channel senders, enable the expanded
+assistant, add tools, disclose credentials or change channel allowlists. The
+native verified-channel integration, per-request authorization and classified
+retrieval are separate activation requirements. Normal `po validate` checks the
+new shape and references; the typed model preserves the fields, and `HUMANS.md`
+shows counterparts when present. Legacy registries retain their existing format.
 
 Installation is manual on all supported OSes (Linux, macOS, Windows). The
